at we have  to do in schools but one of the things  public  officials have to be law enforcement or  those elected to public office  have to  ponder at this moment is what can be  done differently what could be done as  fast as possible  first we need to get to the bottom of  what happened here in this situation  it's obviously i pray for those families  and i hope these numbers do not go up  the death toll numbers but as bill  malugan and others who in his great  reporting earlier what we  what we learned is that the numbers may  go up and even trace gallagher as he  covered this earlier  schools and streets  subways public places like grocery  stores i think we have to be willing to  confront the conversation around guns  and figure out if there are things  sensible things that we can do of course  it's a hard charge and highly  politicized conversation at times but  one thing we know for certain  and i think that your last guess uh the  police former d.c police detective said  it earlier there are too many guns on  the streets this is not a statement  about the second amendment this is just  a statement that too many too many of  the wrong people have guns in their  hands and hire homeless people and  others getting guns in their hands when  they can't feed themselves  and can't can't support themselves but  somehow another can find the money to  buy a gun  again we we need to get to the bottom of  all this that there's a lot of heartfelt  uh condolences and other other things  that are going out to these families in  this community and i certainly don't  want to interrupt that but those in  public life shouldn't shirk their  responsibilities we need to have these  hard uncomfortable conversations about  what we can do to prevent these kinds of  things from happening going forward  molly  you know i do think at times like this  people sort of take comfort in talking  about political answers  to  what's happening at this school and in  so many other mass shootings and that's  fine i mean  restoring peace and order to our society  it is a political question and it does  need to be debated it's also true that  this is evil and that there are things  beyond politics that we need to do we  just seem to be a completely broken  country that does not love one another  the person who committed this horrible  act is responsible alone for what what  happened  but there are bigger issues in play  about how we treat one another  the love we show whether we value human  life and  this is something political but it's  also something much more than political  and i think everybody should  think about the people in their lives  love one another uh think about how to  show love to people that you maybe don't  normally show love to to address the  brokenness and fallenness and to  you know pray for relief from from this  sin that is besieging us you know  throughout the land this is the second  mass shooting in 10 days and it's  untenable what we have here and it's you  know again politics is an appropriate  response but this is something much  deeper there's a moral rot going on that  we all need to  dig in and try to address  thank you panel stand by if you would  hey sean hannity here hey click here to  subscribe to fox news youtube page and  catch our hottest interviews and most  compelling analysis you will not get it  anywhere else
 

